# 4. Accessibility Deep Dive (WCAG 2.1 AA)

### Audit Checklist for Key Flows
| Criterion | Requirement | Implementation |
|-----------|------------|----------------|
| 1.1.1 Non-text Content | Alt text for images, icons | Descriptive alt text, decorative images marked |
| 1.3.1 Info and Relationships | Semantic HTML, ARIA roles | Heading hierarchy, form labels, landmarks |
| 1.4.3 Contrast | 4.5:1 text, 3:1 UI elements | Color palette verification, high-contrast mode |
| 2.1.1 Keyboard | Full keyboard navigation | Tab order, focus indicators, skip links |
| 2.4.7 Focus Visible | Visible focus indicators | Custom focus rings, not outline: none |
| 4.1.2 Name/Role/Value | Screen reader compatibility | ARIA labels, state announcements, live regions |

### Accessibility-First Design Decisions
- Color usage: Never use color alone to convey information
- Typography: Minimum 16px base, support for Dynamic Type / user font scaling
- Touch targets: Minimum 44x44px with adequate spacing
- Motion: Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`, provide alternatives
- Error handling: Clear error messages associated with form fields, not color-only
- Reading order: Logical DOM order matches visual order

### Assistive Technology Testing Plan
- Screen readers: VoiceOver (iOS), TalkBack (Android), NVDA/JAWS (web)
- Keyboard navigation testing
- Switch control testing
- Voice control testing

# 5. Design System Recommendations

### Typography Scale
| Level | Size | Weight | Line Height | Usage |
|-------|------|--------|-------------|-------|
| Display | 32-40px | Bold | 1.2 | Hero sections, splash |
| H1 | 24-28px | Bold | 1.3 | Page titles |
| H2 | 20-22px | Semibold | 1.3 | Section headers |
| Body | 16px | Regular | 1.5 | Primary content |
| Caption | 12-14px | Regular | 1.4 | Labels, metadata |

### Color System
- **Primary**: Brand color for CTAs and key interactive elements
- **Secondary**: Supporting actions, less prominent interactive elements
- **Surface/Background**: Card backgrounds, page backgrounds, elevation levels
- **Semantic**: Success (green), warning (amber), error (red), info (blue) — all meeting contrast ratios
- **Dark mode**: Inverted surfaces, adjusted contrasts, muted primary colors

### Spacing System
- Base unit: 4px or 8px grid
- Component padding: Consistent internal spacing
- Layout margins: Platform-appropriate (16px mobile, 24px tablet, 32px+ desktop)

### Component Library Recommendations
- If React Native: Recommend component library (e.g., NativeBase, React Native Paper, Tamagui)
- If Web: Recommend component library (e.g., Radix, shadcn/ui, Chakra, MUI)
- Custom component needs: What requires custom implementation

# 6. Micro-Interactions & Motion Design

### Key Micro-Interactions
| Interaction | Trigger | Animation | Duration | Purpose |
|-------------|---------|-----------|----------|---------|
| Button press | Tap/click | Scale down 95%, haptic | 100ms | Tactile feedback |
| Page transition | Navigation | Slide / fade | 200-300ms | Context continuity |
| Pull-to-refresh | Swipe down | Spinner animation | Variable | Progress feedback |
| Success action | Task completion | Checkmark + confetti | 400ms | Positive reinforcement |
| Error | Validation fail | Shake + red highlight | 200ms | Error awareness |
| Skeleton loading | Data fetch | Shimmer on shapes | Until loaded | Perceived performance |

### Motion Principles for This Product
- Purposeful: Every animation serves a functional purpose (feedback, orientation, continuity)
- Performance: Animations run at 60fps, use CSS transforms only (no layout thrashing)
- Accessible: All motion can be disabled via `prefers-reduced-motion`
- Consistent: Same type of action = same type of animation throughout the app

# 7. Onboarding & First-Time User Experience

### Onboarding Flow Recommendation
- **Strategy**: Progressive disclosure / tutorial / setup wizard — recommendation with rationale
- **Steps**: Maximum 3-5 steps before first value delivery
- **Skip option**: Always available — users who skip should still be functional
- **Personalization**: What data to collect during onboarding to customize the experience

### First-Run Experience
- What happens the first time a user opens each major screen?
- Empty states that educate and motivate (not just "nothing here yet")
- Sample / demo data to show what the product looks like when populated
- Contextual tooltips for non-obvious features

### Time to Value Target
- Target: User should experience core value within [X minutes] of signing up
- Critical path: [Step 1] → [Step 2] → [Value moment]
- Friction reduction: What steps can be deferred, auto-filled, or skipped?

